        "id": 2640941798,
        "content": "We'll consider this a research exercise and hopefully come up with something interesting. \nIn theory if the services you use have apis then we can monitor webhook events and credit as we do for routine tasks like pull reviews here on GitHub. If you find relevant docs please link them. \nThen you don't need to make these repetitive tasks but instead you'll receive direct rewards based on the actions you took.  \nI suppose that implementing these webhook listeners would make more sense for org functions that require a lot of man power. For example we have like ten developers so it makes sense to automate these things. \nThe next department I would imagine that we might need to scale is more sales related vs lead generation. In which case it most likely would have to deal with parsing meeting transcripts.",
